WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.250
Private payments, parallel blocks, post-quantum signatures: Bitcoin, Kaspa and Monero do not offer all three.

2
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:14.408
With Bitcoin, anyone can trace which addresses were used and which amounts were transferred.

3
00:00:14.408 --> 00:00:16.952
The ledger does not name the key holders.

4
00:00:16.952 --> 00:00:23.590
The QuietBlocks design aims for private payments by default, with proof of one payment whenever you choose.

5
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.162
Kaspa orders blocks in parallel for high layer-one throughput.

6
00:00:28.162 --> 00:00:32.351
A standard payment still shows its inputs, outputs and amounts.

7
00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:42.790
The QuietBlocks design pairs parallel blocks with private payments and targets at least 1,000 accepted private payments per second on layer one for 24 hours.

8
00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:51.214
Monero hides the amount and the recipient, obscures the source, and lets you prove one payment to someone you choose.

9
00:00:51.214 --> 00:00:57.620
Its standard signatures rely on classical elliptic curves, and its blocks form a single chain.

10
00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:05.730
The QuietBlocks design targets at least 128 bits of post-quantum security across the whole system, and parallel blocks.

11
00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.587
This is the research question behind QuietBlocks.

12
00:01:09.587 --> 00:01:16.300
Can one design combine all three, and also protect the origin of a payment from network observers?

13
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:27.079
Side by side, you see that standard payments are public on Bitcoin and Kaspa, Bitcoin and Monero use a single chain, and all three rely on classical signatures.

14
00:01:27.079 --> 00:01:32.090
The QuietBlocks column lists design targets, and no conformant network exists.

15
00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:42.280
Release also requires independent validation and recovery, miners who can choose their own transactions, and a separate review of long-term security funding.

16
00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:49.880
You can read the design, the verification plan and the proposed feasibility study at quietblocks.phexora.ai.
